<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shabaka</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 705 BCE</span> · Also known as Shabako</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shabaka was a king of Kush and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> of the Twenty-fifth Dynasty, who ruled in the late 8th century BCE. Succeeding his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piye">Piye</a>, he conquered the Delta, ended the Twenty-fourth Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sais">Sais</a> and made Memphis a royal residence, uniting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a> under Kushite rule. He restored temples, and the Shabaka Stone, which preserves an ancient Memphite theological text, was carved on his orders.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shabaka.jpg" alt="Shabaka" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: woodsboy2011 · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shabaqa_Sphinx_Head_002.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
